      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Washington State Department of Social Services",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question presented in this case is whether a representative payee, appointed by the commissioner of Social Security, violates the anti-alienation provision of 42 U.S.C., section 407(a), when it uses Social Security benefits to pay for the beneficiary's current maintenance. The plain text of section 407(a) answers this question, and the answer is no."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Can a set-off ever be legal process?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Washington State Department of Social Services",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the department is duly recognized as a representative payee subject to supervision, having to submit constant reports and annual reports and accounting system, and there are audits that have been performed on the department. It is acting in accordance with 405(j) as rep payee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no question that the use of Social Security benefits to pay for current maintenance needs by a beneficiary or by a parent as representative payee is permitted under the Social Security Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Does -- does the State have any set- off rights that private entities don't? Suppose a private person were the representative payee. Do they have the same sort of set-off rights for other debts as the State does?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, I'm just talking about 407 now. I'm just talking about 407. Because the attorney general indicated that the State could, so far as 407 is concerned, set off a tax debt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State argues that section 407(a) doesn't apply to it because it is acting properly as a representative payee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 0.5,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: But -- but your answer to my 407 question talked about 405. I don't -- I don't understand that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Washington",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Washington pays thousands of dollars for these children because they come with psychiatric kinds of needs. We are not paying the minimum. We are, in fact, paying significant amounts of money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1420",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
